  {"ticker": "ONON", "name": "On Holding", "side": "short", "entryDate": "2026-11-13", "entry": 36.06, "exitDate": "", "exit": null, "leverage": 2, "thesis": "Currently trading at 36.06 aftermarket which represents a 9% gain for no apparent reason or news, shorting due to sudden jump."},
  {"ticker": "9984.T", "name": "SoftBank Group", "side": "long", "entryDate": "2026-11-13", "entry": 3738.00, "exitDate": "", "exit": null, "leverage": 1, "thesis": "Holding company whose value rests on its stakes in Arm, SoftBank Corp., the Vision Funds and OpenAI. Shares trade at a discount to the value of those assets after a c. 29% fall over the year. Further gains on its AI holdings, share buybacks and a narrowing of that discount could all lift the price. Key risks: high leverage and results driven by asset revaluations rather than operating profit."},
  {"ticker": "NU", "name": "Nu Holdings (Nubank)", "side": "long", "entryDate": "2026-11-13", "entry": 12.31, "exitDate": "", "exit": null, "leverage": 1, "thesis": "Brazil's presidential runoff on 25 Oct, won by Lula against market expectations, triggered a sharp sell-off in Brazilian assets. Nu fell about 17% the next day and now trades well below its January high, at a much lower earnings multiple than its recent history. With most of its customers in Brazil, the stock was repriced on political risk rather than any change in the business, making this an attractive entry point. Long-term growth comes from continued customer growth and expansion in Mexico and Colombia. Key risks: Brazilian interest rates and fiscal policy, credit quality, and the currency."},
  {"ticker": "MDA", "name": "MDA Space", "side": "long", "entryDate": "2026-11-13", "entry": 29.35, "exitDate": "", "exit": null, "leverage": 1, "thesis": "Recent sell-off offers an attractive entry point: the shares trade roughly 40% below their 52-week high despite revenue growth above 20% and raised 2026 guidance. Net cash of about CAD 1.3bn funds expansion across North America and Europe through the acquisitions of Blue Canyon Technologies (US) and CLS (France). Key risks: a shrinking backlog, weak free cash flow and acquisition integration."},
  {"ticker": "WIZZ.L", "name": "Wizz Air", "side": "short", "entryDate": "2026-11-13", "entry": 1131, "exitDate": "", "exit": null, "leverage": 2, "thesis": "Highly leveraged airline that has swung to a loss: operating profit fell 17% last year, interest is no longer covered by operating profit and current assets do not cover short-term liabilities. Ranked the weakest balance sheet in my screen. Key risks: strong passenger growth, relief on grounded engines and frequent short squeezes."},
  {"ticker": "AAL", "name": "American Airlines", "side": "short", "entryDate": "2026-11-13", "entry": 13.40, "exitDate": "", "exit": null, "leverage": 2, "thesis": "Loss-making with negative shareholders' equity and very thin interest cover. Q3 posted a USD 269m net loss as fuel costs rose 67%, and management guides to a full-year loss. Key risks: revenue growing c. 20%, a fall in oil prices and high short interest (c. 15%) that could fuel a squeeze."}
